add_die_logical_connections
Context: dft (with no sub-context), patterns -ijtag
Mode: setup
Creates a new logical connection data path through a pin on a die instance by specifying the 
source and destination of the logical path. This enables package-level BSDL extraction. You 
can also add logical connections to a die-level BSDL.

list die1/die6_to_tdi die1/die7_to_tdi]
# Add multiple sources with multiple destination pins. In this case, the
#  source and destination pin are matched based on their index in the
#  list. Therefore, the number of pins in each switch should be the same.
add_die_logical_connection \
  -from [list die1/die5_from_tdo die1/die6_from_tdo die1/die7_from_tdo] \
  -to [list die1/die8_to_tdi die1/die9_to_tdi die1/die10_to_tdi] \
  -pipeline_stages 3 \
  -pipeline_safe_values 01x \
  -pipeline_capture_values x01
