analyze_xbounding
Context: dft -scan, dft (with no sub-context)
Mode: analysis
Performs X-bounding analysis.
Usage
analyze_xbounding [-force -reset]
Description
For RTL designs, run this command in the dft (no sub-context) context, and for gate-level 
designs, use the dft -scan context.
This command identifies memory elements (current scan cells or cells that will be converted to 
scan in a subsequent run) that might capture an unknown value during logic BIST. In addition, 
the command identifies where to place bounding muxes that prevent these X-sources from 
reaching the memory elements and corrupting the signature during logic BIST. For more 
information, refer to “X-Bounding” in the Hybrid TK/LBIST Flow User’s Manual.
The X-bounding analysis uses the E5 DRC to identify and bound all X sources from reaching 
scan cells and corrupting the MISR. All primary inputs and internal X source pins (for example, 
non scan cells, blackbox outputs pins) are x-bounded.

