To extract ICL when the clock gater has an ICL Clock port in its fanout, model the clock gater 
as follow:
Module cgand {
  Attribute use_in_icl_extraction = "when_reached_by_other_modules";
  ClockPort CK;
  ToClockPort GCK {
    Source mux;
  }
  DataInPort FE;
  ClockMux mux SelectedBy FE {
    1'b0 : 1'b0;
    1'b1 : CK;
  }
}
If an iProc calls iClock on a ClockPort that is in the fanout of the clock gater and you did not set 
the DFT signal my_clock_en to 1, the tool issues this error:
//  Error: Unable to trace iClock 'sub1.clk' to top module input port.
//  Encountered a constant ICL source connection 'cgand1.mux' while
//  tracing clock source.
If the clock gater was not modeled in ICL, the tool would not report this issue, and the problem 
would only show up during simulation.
