• -maskfile_pattern_offset number
An optional switch and integer that specify the pattern offset number for the mask file. By 
default (when no offset is specified), the pattern in the mask file starts with pattern 0. This 
switch is useful for reducing the number of pattern files that must be loaded when only a 
subset need to be masked. For more information, refer to Example 2.
• -preserve_masked_observe_points
An optional switch that enables you to preserve existing masked observation points 
(wherever Xs appear in a pattern’s unload and measure_po values) in external patterns 
loaded into the tool. When you use this switch to preserve existing masked observation 
points in the external patterns, the internal patterns stored after simulating the external 
patterns preserve these masked observation points. You can optionally use -mask_file to 
specify additional observation points to be masked.

