Examples
Example 1
Assume the tool is in setup mode. The following example reports, for a design with two scan 
channels and no shared EDT pins, the names and inversion status of the EDT pins. The example 
then shares the EDT clock pin with a functional pin called “a1”. Following that, it renames the 
dedicated EDT bypass pin from the default name to “my_bypass” and specifies in the same 
command that the bypass signal is inverted between the chip input pin and the EDT logic. 
Afterward, the example again reports the EDT pins. 
report_edt_pins
// 
//    Pin description         Pin name           Inversion  
//    ---------------         --------           ---------  
//    Clock                   edt_clock              - 
