Example 7
You can override enum parameters when they are not locally defined within a module. Given 
the following code:
package pkg1;
typedef enum {red, green, blue} colors_t;
endpackage
typedef enum {pink, yellow, cyan} topcolor_t;
module top (input logic clk,
input logic resetn);
parameter pkg1::colors_t my_pkg_enum = pkg1::blue;
parameter topcolor_t my_enum = cyan
endmodule
You can override the my_pkg_enum parameter with the set_current_design command:
SETUP> set_current_design top -parameter_values {my_pkg_enum pkg1::green}
You cannot override the my_enum parameter because it is defined within the top module. For 
example, the following set_current_design command produces an error:
SETUP> set_current_design top -parameter_values {my_enum yellow}
Error: Not able to create a parameterized view for module/entity 'top'. 
Overwriting enum parameter 'my_enum', where enum is defined within a 
module, is not supported.

