Example 11
The following example shows how to specify user annotations and how the annotations appear 
in STIL, WGL, and Verilog formats.
This command supplies the user annotations directly:
write_patterns … -user_annotation {line1 {line2   with spaces} line3}
This pair of commands uses a variable to supply the user annotations. The effect is identical to 
the previous command:
set annotations {line1 {line2   with spaces} line3}
write_patterns … -user_annotation $annotations
Both of the preceding command sequences produce the following output in these formats 
(shown with the Verify section for context):
• STIL
History {
   Ann {*  Begin_Verify_Section  *}
   Ann {*  End_Verify_Section  *}
   Ann {*  Begin_Verify_Section  *}
   Ann {*  Begin_User_Annotation_Section *}
   Ann {*     line1 *}
   Ann {*     line2   with spaces *}
   ANN {*     line3 *}
   Ann {*  End_UserAnnotation_Section  *}
}
