The last two lines indicate the procedure named “capture1” forces a 1 on the internal pin /inst_0/
QI_nx7, but the value produced on the pin when simulated in the Verilog simulator is 0. This 
suggests the force statement is applying an incorrect value. The next example shows what the 
corresponding force statement (highlighted in bold) might look like in the test procedure file:
procedure capture capture1 =
scan_group groupcnt ;
mode internal = 
timeplate gen_tp1 ;
cycle =
force clear 0 ;
force clock[0] 0 ;
...
force clock[9] 0 ;
force test_clk 0 ;
force /inst_0/QI_nx7 1;
force_pi ;
measure_po ;
pulse clock[0] ;
...
pulse clock[4] ;
end;
end;
