Checks that the connections between the EDT or uncompressed scan chains connect only to a 
single SSH.
The following lists the checks and the violations that may occur: 
• If any channel of an EDT instance connects to an SSH instance, all channels of that 
instance must connect to that SSH instance. There cannot be a mix of SSH and non-SSH 
connections to the EDT instance.
The error message is:
//  Error: SSN is active but EDT instance 'edt_inst'
//         is not correctly connected to a single SSH
//         instance. (SSN_R4-1)
Where ‘edt_inst’ is the EDT instance name. 
• For uncompressed chains, the scan chain should be connected to a single SSH instance.
The error message is:
//  Error: SSN is active but scan chain 'chain_1'
//         is not correctly connected to a single SSH
//         instance. (SSN_R4-1)
Where ‘chain_1’ is a scan chain name. 
