Clocking
A wrapper that specifies the information used by the EDT controller clock. 
Usage
DftSpecification(module_name,id) {
EDT {
Controller(id) {
Clocking { 
type           : edge | level ;
lockup_cells   : on | off ;
reset_signal   : auto | asynchronous | off | ijtag_reset ;
reset_polarity : auto | active_low | active_high ;
}
}
}
}
Arguments
• type : edge | level ;
An optional property that determines what type of architecture logic EDT uses. The default 
is edge. This property is equivalent to the “-CLocking” argument in the set_edt_options 
command. The following are the possible values:
o edge — Specifies DFF-based logic. You can use DFF-based logic for designs that 
are LSSD-based, mux-DFF-based, or that incorporate a mixture of these two 
architectures.
o level — Specifies latch-based logic. This option is for pure LSSD designs only.
Restriction
An error message is issued if you specify the type as level when the EDT controller 
is connected to an SSH.

