A set of properties that specify the port names associated with each function on the TDO 
multiplexer module, as well as on the TAP controller itself. See the Usage section for a list 
of the functions and their default values.
Note
The TDO multiplexer module contains two control ports: ir_select and 
bypass_devid_select. These ports are not combined in the TAP module to satisfy 
ICL modeling rules. IJTAG does not permit combining IRSelect with a Data signal, so 
they must remain separate to the TDO multiplexer. The ICL module models this as two 
cascaded multiplexers, whereas the Verilog module combines them.

