Description
A wrapper that specifies different boundary scan chain configurations based on bonding 
variations in the cores of a design. Use this wrapper to bypass certain parts of the boundary scan 
chain in the cores.
Arguments
• name
A string that uniquely identifies each bonding configuration. 
• enable_signal : pin_or_net_name ;
A property that specifies a signal inside the design that is 1 when the given bonding 
configuration is used, and 0 for all other bonding configurations.
The pin_or_net_name can be a DftSignal(name) that you previously registered with the 
register_static_dft_signal_names command as a global DFT control signal and added with 
the add_dft_signals command.
You must ensure the enable_signal has the correct value during simulation. The current 
enable_signal should be 1 and all others 0. If it is a DftSignal, you can use the Patterns/
DftControlSettings property to set the value. For a pin or net, you are responsible for setting 
the value during simulation.
You must specify an enable signal if you define bypassed_logical_groups or 
active_logical_groups.
Note
The tool does not create the enable signal if it is not already present in the design and 
the DftSpecification/allow_port_creation_on_current_design property is off.

