Description
The PostScanActivityControl wrapper is an optional wrapper defined within the LogicBIST 
controller wrapper that configures the hybrid TL/LBIST post-scan activity. You can build the 
hardware to let the controller run continuously to keep the power from dropping after the last 
scan pattern is applied. This is useful when you are running many controllers in parallel, and 
you do not want the power to drop between the time that one controller stops and the next 
controller starts.
A second type of post-scan activity enables a number of post-scan patterns to be applied so that 
the power can gradually settle rather than drop abruptly.
Arguments
• activity_type :auto | none | cooldown | unlimited;
An optional property that specifies the type of post-scan activity to use. When set to 
unlimited, the controller keeps running continuously after the specified number of patterns 
has completed. When set to cooldown, the CoolDownPatternCount/max property specifies 
how many extra patterns are run.
When this property is set to auto, it resolves to cooldown if the CoolDownPatternCount 
wrapper is present; otherwise, it resolves to none.
• CoolDownPatternType/max : int;
An optional property that specifies the maximum number of cool-down patterns for the 
controller. This is equivalent to “set_lbist_controller_options 
-max_cooldown_pattern_count.” The default is 255 when activity_type is set to cooldown, 
and 0 otherwise.

port_name ;
An optional property that specifies the name of an external LBIST enable port. The default 
is ext_lbist_en.
Examples
The following example renames LogicBIST ports back to their pre-2018.1 release versions for 
purposes of backwards annotation.
