When unspecified, it defaults to a null string that is interpreted as the common instance 
ancestor of all memory controllers driven by the memory BIST BAP. See the description of 
the get_common_parent_instance command to see how the common ancestor is computed. 
When inst_path is specified as “.”, the memory BIST BAP is instantiated in the top module 
of the design.
This property is not used or needed when the process_dft_specification command is run 
with the -no_insertion option.

