Description
The BisrChainAccessOptions wrapper specifies the options that control BISR chain operations. 
This wrapper can be used at all design levels (specifically, top, block, or sub-block level). To 
use the BisrChainAccessOptions wrapper, you must specify MemoryBisr/run_mode : 
bisr_chain_access. The bisr_chain_access run mode always performs a shift operation on the 
entire BISR chain. If you must preserve the contents of the BISR chain, the enable_rotation 
property should be enabled; otherwise, the shift operation clears the contents of the BISR chain 
when it completes.
You specify access to individual BISR registers using the BisrRegisterAccessOptions. Any 
read_value or write_value specified in this wrapper overrides the default_read_value and 
default_write_value specified in the BisrChainAccessOptions wrapper.

