Description
The ManufacturingOptions wrapper is used in the Defaults/PatternsSpecification wrapper.
Arguments
• max_async_clock_sources : integer | unlimited ;
A property that specifies how many asynchronous clocks can be active within one Patterns 
wrapper. Modern testers can generate multiple asynchronous clocks. Use this property to 
control how many instruments, belonging to different asynchronous frequency groups, can 
be executed in parallel. 
If you specify an integer, Tessent Shell creates memory BIST patterns that use no more than 
the specified number of asynchronous clocks. Valid integer values are 0 or greater. When 
you specify a value of 0, all clocks used in the pattern are synchronous. Use the value of 0 
when the tester does not have any asynchronous clock generators.

