Description
A wrapper used in metadata to define a repeatable property that is usable in configuration data.
As opposed to normal properties, a repeatable property has no default values and does not exist 
until it is specified. 
Arguments
• Usage : normal | hidden | Env(EnvVar) ;
A property that controls the visibility of a property. When set to normal, the property is 
reported by report_config_syntax and visible in the Config Data Browser. When set to 
hidden, the wrapper is not reported by report_config_syntax and invisible in the Config 
Data Browser. Its value can still be fetched and edited using the configuration introspection 
and editing commands such as the get_config_value command if the name of the hidden 
property is known to you. The “Usage : Env(EnvVar)” is treated as normal if the EnvVar 
environment variable is defined and set to 1; otherwise it is treated as hidden.

