Examples
The normal WaveformChar set for a bidi port permits all possible operations for the port. The 
following is a sample Waveform definition for a bidi pin in the WaveformTable:
bidi_time_gen_0    { LHXT { '0ns' Z; '30ns' L/H/X/T; }
                     01Z  { '0ns' D/U/Z; } }
The green characters on both lines are the WaveformChars. For the first line, they correspond to 
measure events at 30 ns for compare low (L), compare high (H), compare unknown (X), and 
compare high-impedance (T). At 0 ns, the input side of the bidi port is forced off (Z). For the 
second line, the 01Z WaveformChars correspond to force down (D), force up (U), and force off 
(Z) at 0 ns.

