SystemVerilog Generic Interface Port Declarations 
in the Root Module of a Child Block
In a bottom-up flow SystemVerilog generic interface port declarations cannot be used in the 
root module of a child block or core.
The following example illustrates a generic interface port:
module mem1 (interface pins, input clk);
…
endmodule
