Note - Viewing PDF files within a web browser causes some links not to function. Use HTML for full navigation.
SystemVerilog Interfaces in Task or Function 
Invocation
Multiple arguments which are defined as instantiations of the same SV interface type cannot be 
passed in a single task or function invocation. For example:
interface my_intf #( parameter SZ1 = 1);
wire w1[SZ1-1: 0];
wire w2[SZ1-1: 0];
// some logic around w1,w2 etc…
endinterface
my_intf #(10) intf_obj_1;
my_intf #(20) intf_obj_2;
…
// Single function,task call using objects of same interface
   my_func (intf_obj_1, intf_obj_2, <other_arguments>);
… 
The work around is to uniquify the instantiations of the interface as follows:
interface my_intf #( parameter SZ1 = 1);
  wire w1[SZ1-1: 0];
  wire w2[SZ1-1: 0];
// some logic around w1,w2 etc…
endinterface
interface my_intf_1 #( parameter SZ1 = 1);
  wire w1[SZ1-1: 0];
  wire w2[SZ1-1: 0];
// some logic around w1,w2 etc…
endinterface
my_intf #(10) intf_obj_1;
my_intf_1 #(20) intf_obj_2;
…
// Single function,task call using objects of different interfaces
   my_func (intf_obj_1, intf_obj_2, <other_arguments>);
…
